  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Access to Justice for Victims of Gender Discrimination</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite legislation to the contrary, women and girls in Kenya do not experience equal rights, facing discrimination in many areas of life, including education, health, property rights, employment, violence, access to justice. The recent Constitution and Bill of Rights provides an opportunity to tackle the lack of awareness of what counts as discrimination and how women can access their rights to equal treatment under the law. This project will train local organisations across Kenya in how to recognise cases of gender discrimination, how to support and advise the women to get redress. Local lawyers will be trained in equal rights law, and will represent complex cases in the courts. The legal advice service will be publicised, so communities become aware of the issues and the solutions. Some cases will be identified as appropriate for strategic litigation, to be taken through the courts to establish precedents, to ensure that the commitments of the Bill of Rights are made real.  As a result, women&apos;s opportunities and lives will have improved, and local organisations and lawyers will be equipped to help other women in the future, while the issues will be more widely known. Women&apos;s rights will have been made more real.</narrative>
  </description>
